WEBVTT

00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:09.770
<i>Back then, I didn't want to be
at school, home, or anywhere else.</i>

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.330
<i>I simply sat in a pitch-black place,
holding my knees.</i>

00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.820
A very good evening to
all those who have tuned in.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.490
I'm your host, Kaiyu.

00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:24.150
Tonight, we'll be saving more lost lambs
wandering around our city.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:27.710
Yes, indeed. It's time for FM Hagoromo's
"The Seven Sages' Life Advice".

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:33.790
Vent your troubles at your aging elders.
That's all this program is about.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.630
Now, our first caller tonight
is actually speaking to us live!

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.150
Good evening. Please introduce yourself.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:43.060
What's in a name?

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.180
So you're a no-name, just like FM 77.4.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:48.350
Please wait your turn, Sukekiyo-san!

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:50.730
How old are you, miss?

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:52.860
Fourteen.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.120
You must be in the third year
of junior high, then?

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.520
I don't go to school all that much.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:00.090
What kind of advice are you looking for tonight?

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:02.610
I want to die.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:06.390
What a coincidence. I've been thinking
it's about time for me to go as well.

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.080
We've lived too long, haven't we?

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:12.960
No need to rush.
The reaper will come for us soon enough.

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:15.780
Don't lump me in with you! I seriously—

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.760
Times like these call for booze!

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.970
Someone bring Sadakichi-san some cloudy sake!

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:21.920
Cut it out. We're live on air!

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:23.340
We're more sober when drunk.

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:27.350
Once you reach drinking age,
you can drown yourself in alcohol.

00:01:27.730 --> 00:01:30.040
And what if I still want to die?

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.900
That's what you call a hangover.

00:01:31.900 --> 00:01:34.540
What the hell? Are you messing with me?

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:36.760
That's what life is all about.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.150
If you've lost all hope in the world around you,

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:42.410
then why don't you try
seeing it in a different light?

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:46.730
The value of a jewel is determined
by the light shining upon it.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:49.670
That goes for the world in your eyes, too.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:56.000
The wedding ring I gave my late wife
had a small but dazzling jewel, too...

00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:31.640
<i>A new school year has begun.</i>

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:36.450
<i>With the addition of Gotou-san and other freshmen,
we now have twenty-three members.</i>

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:41.740
<i>Just as Serizawa-san advised,
we're aiming for gold in Category B.</i>

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.660
<i>And today, we have a joint practice
with the famous Fujigasaki High.</i>

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:53.150
<i>Witnessing the part practice and ensemble
rehearsal of a powerhouse would motivate us...</i>

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:55.880
<i>or so we thought.</i>

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:57.520
Your tone is all over the place!

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.510
Pay attention to the directions!

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:05.590
I can't believe how much they get
yelled at despite being that good.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:08.760
Well, yeah, we're nowhere close to
being as good and we're already stuck.

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.930
I kept hitting the wrong notes.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:14.390
Maren and Narushima stuck out like a sore thumb.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:16.250
Yeah.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:19.020
Kamijou-kun tried to bridge the gap
between us and the rest, but...

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:21.820
Don't fret, my hard worker.
You've got nothing to be ashamed of.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:25.200
Oh, right. I'm collecting happiness koalas
from Koala's March in a bottle.

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.530
I'll share them with you.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.740
You were surprisingly calm
when it mattered, Homura.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.660
Even when you make a mistake,
you manage to stay calm.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:34.210
Well, Chika-chan's really
shameless, if nothing else.

00:04:35.970 --> 00:04:39.130
Let's figure out what we have to do
and drill it into our very bones.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:44.640
I'll practise more so that
I don't hold you two back.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.050
I'll work twice as hard! Four times, if need be!

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:50.520
We'll need to practise after school
every weekday and start early every weekend.

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:51.350
Got it.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.500
Okay!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:53.640
About that...

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:56.810
I'm thinking of placing restrictions
on your practice hours.

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.070
Sure, the All-Japans are important,
and so is getting to Fumon Hall,

00:05:00.070 --> 00:05:03.570
but your life after that is much more important.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:08.210
If the second- and third-years don't score
at least the average on their midterms,

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.620
I'll cut practice time on Sundays
and after 6PM on weekdays.

00:05:14.470 --> 00:05:18.330
Why did Kusakabe-sensei suddenly bring that up?

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:22.750
You three will be fine because
you're in the top 20 of our year, but I...

00:05:23.230 --> 00:05:25.260
Are you going to have trouble
hitting the average mark?

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.220
A little bit, yeah...

00:05:28.220 --> 00:05:30.380
I'll get mad if you don't make the cut, okay?

00:05:30.380 --> 00:05:31.520
What?!

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:33.180
Fine. I'll do my best.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:38.170
I'm gonna take this all the way!

00:05:39.220 --> 00:05:40.440
My...

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:43.110
All the way!

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.930
<i>All the way...</i>

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:53.240
Well, I can't concentrate when it's too quiet.

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:58.330
Looks like it started on time tonight.

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:58.710
Tonight, we'll be saving more lost lambs
wandering around our city.

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:01.660
It's time for FM Hagoromo's
"The Seven Sages' Life Advice".

00:06:01.660 --> 00:06:07.570
Here in the studio, our seven life specialists
are eagerly awaiting their turn.

00:06:07.570 --> 00:06:12.270
Picture seven chihuahuas that finally found
someone to play with after a week of boredom.

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.180
They can be pretty annoying.

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:14.790
Heh, chihuahuas.

00:06:14.790 --> 00:06:16.700
Let's get right to tonight's first client.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:21.120
He works for a local IT company and
goes by the alias of Corporate Dog.

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.650
What is IT?

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:25.630
It stands for "information technology".

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.020
Stands for what?

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:28.960
Japanese, son. Do you speak it?

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:32.090
Fine! Just think of it as standing
for Incan Tawantinsuyu!

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:33.200
He threw in the towel.

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:35.580
The civilisation that fell to ruin
because it arrogantly believed

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:38.080
that knowledge was not to
be shared with commoners?

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:38.980
It's like that too.

00:06:38.980 --> 00:06:40.920
He threw in the towel,
but they threw it back at him!
It's like that too.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:41.290
It's like that too.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.130
Anyway, moving on.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:45.220
"I work overtime every day,
and even come to work on holidays,

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:48.050
so I've lost touch with my friends
and can't get a girlfriend.

00:06:48.050 --> 00:06:52.840
Unable to live a normal human life, I worry about
my future prospects. What should I do?

00:06:53.590 --> 00:06:57.390
Sadakichi-san, what's a normal human life, anyway?

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.040
Being able to get a good night's sleep.

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:00.980
That's it, really.

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.650
Okay, I'll try to do that too!

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:07.440
Next up, we have a caller speaking to us live!

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.670
My, it's been a while since we last had a caller.

00:07:10.670 --> 00:07:15.560
Reminds you of the junior high girl who called
and said she wanted to die, doesn't it?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:17.860
Alias: "Desert Rabbit".

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:18.640
Hello.

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.910
You sent in a postcard last time, right?

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:25.370
You're the one who fell in love with
the same person as a clubmate, yes?

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:28.840
If memory serves, the target of your
unrequited love was your club advisor.

00:07:29.390 --> 00:07:30.320
That's right.

00:07:30.320 --> 00:07:33.760
Your don't wanna hurt your rival
cause they're your BFF, right?

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:37.810
But I'd rather fillet them
than have my love stolen away.

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:40.080
Oh, I remember!

00:07:40.080 --> 00:07:43.890
You said you were socially
at a disadvantage, correct?

00:07:43.890 --> 00:07:45.610
What happened after that?

00:07:45.610 --> 00:07:47.930
I'm here to confess tonight.

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:49.650
Actually, due to a scheme of mine,

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:55.150
my rival, who doesn't have the best grades,
was forced to neglect club and study.

00:07:55.150 --> 00:07:56.830
I feel kinda bad.

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.280
Haruta?!

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:03.760
"Fillet"? You feel "kinda bad"?!

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:05.540
Sorry, Chika-chan.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:08.090
What was that all about?

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:11.260
I spoke to Kusakabe-sensei alone the other day.

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:13.900
He was worried about our futures.

00:08:13.900 --> 00:08:17.470
You know how he makes this
pained expression at times like that?

00:08:18.010 --> 00:08:20.640
It made my heart race for some reason.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.450
So I offered a little suggestion...

00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:25.120
Your heart raced, did it?
More like you stole yet another march on me!

00:08:25.120 --> 00:08:27.750
You owe me an apology.
I was actually studying seriously.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:30.510
Seriously? Weren't you listening to the radio?

00:08:32.290 --> 00:08:34.600
When did you start tuning in to that program?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.800
Right after I joined high school.

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:39.860
Apparently, that local radio station
was originally established by the city.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:42.720
A private party took over
and now runs it on a reduced scale.

00:08:42.720 --> 00:08:47.000
Oh, so that's why it only plays the sound
of waves and whatnot during the day.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:51.800
It seems that "The Seven Sages'
Life Advice" started two years ago.

00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.090
The "sages" are seven senior citizens,

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:57.310
and they've never revealed where
the program is broadcast from.

00:08:57.310 --> 00:08:59.800
The address they give out
for postcards is a P.O. Box, too.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:05.100
For some reason, it feels like a hidden village
straight out of Japanese folklore to me.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:06.680
A hidden village?

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:07.070
Freeze!
A hidden village?

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:10.150
Without troubling or hurting anyone,

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.780
Kaiyu and the Seven Sages
live quietly in the radio program.

00:09:14.780 --> 00:09:18.140
I get the feeling they should be left well alone.

00:09:21.370 --> 00:09:23.160
I've got a bad feeling about this.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:24.580
Are you listening to me?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.660
Y-Yeah...

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.080
Hey, Homura!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:30.470
President Hinohara?

00:09:31.330 --> 00:09:33.380
Surely it's just one of the
biology club's chickens.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:35.360
Oh, Kamijou?

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:36.550
Perfect.

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.840
Jeez.

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:40.160
You're interrupting our morning practice.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:42.830
The concert band's budget
for this year has been decided.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:47.490
This is brutal.

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.060
Unbelievable!

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.400
Can you blame us? You've achieved nothing.

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:52.720
Ow!

00:09:53.460 --> 00:09:55.020
Don't be hasty!

00:09:55.020 --> 00:09:56.690
I came to offer you a lifeboat.

00:09:57.070 --> 00:09:58.610
I bet it's full of holes.

00:09:58.610 --> 00:10:03.280
If you can solve a certain pending issue for me,
I'll add 200,000 yen to your budget.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:04.640
200,000?!

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:07.960
One of the culture clubs has
declined its funding for this year.

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:09.400
They turned down 200,000 yen?!

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.830
Which club was that?

00:10:11.310 --> 00:10:13.220
The geological research club.

00:10:13.220 --> 00:10:17.000
If you can catch its president and
bring her to the student council office,

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:21.010
I'll negotiate for her to give you those funds.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.440
I smell something fishy!

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:24.370
Speak.

00:10:24.370 --> 00:10:27.800
Why'd the geological research
club decline their funding?

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:29.940
Why is its president on the run?

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:34.860
I'll give you the rest of the story after school,
so elect some representatives.

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.930
We offer you our lively young girl.

00:10:37.610 --> 00:10:40.910
Why do I have to chase after
some helmet-wearing weirdo?

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:43.620
You know her, Senpai?

00:10:43.620 --> 00:10:46.040
No way! No chance! Absolutely not!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.400
Be a man and admit it.

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:49.210
But I'm a girl! And I'm busy!

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.540
"I'm busy" is the kind of excuse dumbass
old men with too much free time use.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.520
Apologise to fathers all across the country!

00:10:56.520 --> 00:10:59.760
Don't you want to buy
instruments for the newcomers?

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:01.550
We're counting on you, Homura-san!

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.050
Save the concert band!

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:06.520
All right, all right.

00:11:06.520 --> 00:11:07.850
But <i>he's</i> coming with me.

00:11:08.630 --> 00:11:10.270
I knew it.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:14.950
Her name is Asou Misato. She's in Class 2-5.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:17.110
The geology club has eight members.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:20.400
They show crazy unity under Asou, the president.

00:11:21.310 --> 00:11:24.200
She's also one of the student council blacklist's top ten.

00:11:24.200 --> 00:11:25.960
Another oddball, huh?

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:27.250
Very pretty.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:31.910
She's narrowed down the club's objectives
to mining precious stones.

00:11:31.910 --> 00:11:34.470
Can you even mine precious stones in Japan?

00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.470
You can find quite a few kinds, actually.

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:37.630
But only in small quantities.

00:11:38.270 --> 00:11:41.670
Trespassing on private properties
to mine is a crime, though.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:44.470
So how are they achieving anything?

00:11:44.470 --> 00:11:46.930
By using the geology department
at the prefectural university.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.810
They performed a thorough
survey of the city on foot.

00:11:50.260 --> 00:11:53.220
Going by the timing of and channels used
in the distribution of granitic pegmatite,

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:56.880
they identified places likely
to have traces of rainbow garnet

00:11:56.880 --> 00:11:58.820
and got the university moving.

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:00.990
Grammatical pragmatic...

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:02.950
Don't strain yourself.

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:07.730
Apparently, they handed the rainbow garnet
they discovered over to the university.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:12.920
In return, the university agreed to cover
all of the geology club's operating costs.

00:12:12.920 --> 00:12:15.610
So that's why they declined the funding.

00:12:15.610 --> 00:12:19.130
Well, they're the sort of people who'd rather
not use even a single yen of school money.

00:12:19.590 --> 00:12:21.210
Why?

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.140
Because they hate school.

00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:23.760
What?

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:28.300
They're a bunch of kids who'd never
come to school if it weren't for their club.

00:12:28.800 --> 00:12:33.030
The geological research club
is a group of former shut-ins.

00:12:33.030 --> 00:12:34.400
I see.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:38.310
Asou created the GeoClub,
contacted shut-in students,

00:12:38.310 --> 00:12:42.280
and successfully got them to come
to school using club activities.

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.390
How'd she pull off that miracle?

00:12:44.390 --> 00:12:46.700
She barged into their homes
and straight up talked them into it.

00:12:47.730 --> 00:12:51.910
The goddess of fate who would change
their lives descended upon them, huh?

00:12:53.310 --> 00:12:57.090
I need you, no matter what.
Lend me your strength.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:01.880
Apparently, a male student named Hiyama
was the only one who didn't agree.

00:13:02.260 --> 00:13:03.100
Hiyama?

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:06.590
But why is that goddess on the run?

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:08.470
Asou and gang outdid themselves this year.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:11.930
They found a mineral more valuable
than rainbow garnet.

00:13:11.930 --> 00:13:13.370
Is she some kind of genius?

00:13:13.370 --> 00:13:19.010
But after that, Asou sent the uni a blunt email
and hasn't contacted them since.

00:13:20.350 --> 00:13:22.980
And what were they supposed to mine this year?

00:13:23.470 --> 00:13:24.660
Topaz.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:26.410
Natural blue topaz.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:30.190
Also known as the jewel of the setting sun.

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.870
So you're having curry tonight?

00:13:37.870 --> 00:13:40.200
I had a feeling it might be that.

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:42.470
Here you go. I'll bring you a spoon right away.

00:13:42.470 --> 00:13:46.590
No need, Mrs. Homura.
I've brought my own, eco-friendly chopsticks.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.760
I scoop the rice, but it slips from my grasp.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.930
It's almost like Chika-chan's first love.

00:13:51.300 --> 00:13:52.720
Isn't it hard to eat that way?

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:55.260
Did you just come to bum dinner off us?

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.920
Nah. I wanted to talk about Asou-san.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.650
Why is she running around like that?

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.970
They found the place where the blue topaz rests.

00:14:03.970 --> 00:14:05.940
But they don't want anyone to know where.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:07.210
And why is that?

00:14:07.210 --> 00:14:09.200
We'll have to catch her and ask.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:10.660
Uh, Mrs. Homura,

00:14:11.060 --> 00:14:12.800
I could use that spoon right about now.

00:14:12.800 --> 00:14:14.240
Should we catch her?

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:18.540
The GeoClub is a refuge Asou-san built.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:23.670
And she herself was truant
through most of junior high.

00:14:23.670 --> 00:14:26.210
She must have a reason she can't talk about.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:27.520
It's too late.

00:14:27.520 --> 00:14:32.110
President Katagari apparently already
sent her a challenge via Hinohara-san.

00:14:32.110 --> 00:14:33.880
Did she respond?

00:14:33.880 --> 00:14:35.850
"Bring it. Over."

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.270
Asou!

00:14:37.840 --> 00:14:38.730
Where are you?!

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.670
Asou Misato-san?

00:14:40.670 --> 00:14:41.810
Are you here?

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:50.410
Here it is.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:52.670
Asou-san, you there?

00:14:53.450 --> 00:14:54.530
She's going to run!

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:55.360
Let's barge in!

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:57.040
Why do you have the key?

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.960
I borrowed it from the staff room!

00:15:09.770 --> 00:15:11.630
Climb up, Yasu!

00:15:11.630 --> 00:15:15.970
You're an imperial soldier fated
to die one step away from his goal!

00:15:15.970 --> 00:15:18.140
Asou-san tunes in as well?

00:15:18.140 --> 00:15:20.640
FM Hagoromo. Frequency 77.4.

00:15:21.700 --> 00:15:26.270
Do you remember what Hinohara-san said about there
being a male student who Asou-san couldn't woo?

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:28.940
I got a little curious, so I looked him up.

00:15:29.530 --> 00:15:32.360
His name is Hiyama Kaiyuu.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.740
Kaiyuu?

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:35.030
Kaiyu?!

00:15:35.990 --> 00:15:38.830
"I found it, but I'm pretending I didn't."

00:15:39.230 --> 00:15:41.280
I thought about what that message meant.

00:15:41.280 --> 00:15:42.250
And what does it mean?

00:15:43.160 --> 00:15:49.460
If I'm right, then she ended up finding
the hidden village in this city too.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:56.100
I was really surprised to find you'd become
acquainted with the geological research club.

00:15:56.100 --> 00:15:58.280
You know about it?

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:01.310
Asou-san is pretty famous
among the teachers here.

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:06.990
We should end this game of tag as soon
as possible for Asou-san's sake too.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.540
Sorry for calling you out like this.

00:16:14.540 --> 00:16:15.110
It's okay.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:18.580
These two are Kamijou-kun and
Homura-san from the concert band.

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:22.670
I hear you like jewels.

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:28.630
Crystals turn sunlight into
something more beautiful.

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:31.390
Sunlight?

00:16:31.390 --> 00:16:33.750
Someone once taught me

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:37.470
that if you have a hard time in
the outside world or lose all hope,

00:16:37.470 --> 00:16:41.140
you have to try seeing it in a different light.

00:16:42.150 --> 00:16:43.580
Asou-san...

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.440
The blue topaz, radio, and Hiyama Kaiyuu

00:16:46.440 --> 00:16:49.230
are all connected, aren't they?

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:53.520
While you were protecting
a colony within this school,

00:16:53.520 --> 00:16:58.530
there was a boy the same age as you
desperately protecting a colony of his own.

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:04.310
Your pursuit of blue topaz
took you to where he was...

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:09.630
An unregistered retirement home.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:14.150
Asou-san.

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:18.230
We're listeners who tune
into that radio station too.

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.320
You know, "The Seven Sages' Life Advice".

00:17:21.260 --> 00:17:23.400
Haruta's asked them for advice several times.

00:17:23.400 --> 00:17:26.170
I think his alias was, uh, Desert—

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:26.850
Chika-chan!

00:17:27.380 --> 00:17:29.440
Quit running your mouth!

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:30.770
Like it matters!

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:32.160
It totally does!

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:34.560
Huh? Oh, right, ahaha...

00:17:34.560 --> 00:17:36.070
Don't "ahaha" me!

00:17:36.070 --> 00:17:38.320
You have zero tact!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:39.300
Hey, it's a little more than that!

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:40.920
Not after you round it down, it isn't!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:42.660
Want me to make a fillet out of you?

00:17:42.660 --> 00:17:44.580
I swear I'll never target you
with my schemes again!

00:17:44.580 --> 00:17:45.540
Haruta!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:46.660
I said I'm sorry!

00:17:50.980 --> 00:17:51.500
Yes?

00:17:52.150 --> 00:17:56.590
I'm Kusakabe Shinjirou from
Shimizu Minami High. I called earlier.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:03.000
Hiyama Kaiyuu-kun, yes?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.290
Sorry.

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:11.560
And sorry I couldn't join you
even though you came so many times.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:15.090
Are you guys my classmates?

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:18.080
Nah. We didn't get that opportunity.

00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:20.900
Oh, right. I got held back.

00:18:20.900 --> 00:18:22.360
This is kinda weird.

00:18:22.870 --> 00:18:25.160
Hearing your voice in person.

00:18:26.320 --> 00:18:30.210
We three have been listening to you for ages.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:32.290
Radio host Kaiyu.

00:18:33.430 --> 00:18:34.990
I've always wanted to meet you.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:43.200
The people here all either
fell out with their families

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:46.440
or had nobody to talk to
because they lived alone.

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:51.080
At some point, we started looking
after those people in our annex.

00:18:51.080 --> 00:18:54.200
But why'd you start operating a radio station?

00:18:54.200 --> 00:18:59.950
Someone my dad helped in the past was
on FM Hagoromo's board. He helped us out.

00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:03.620
Since we were trying to hide from society,

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:06.850
he probably wanted to provide us
with a connection to it.

00:19:07.290 --> 00:19:09.670
You sure think about some complicated things.

00:19:10.440 --> 00:19:11.810
You had fun, didn't you?

00:19:12.850 --> 00:19:14.960
Yeah, it was fun.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:18.630
We found something to do together
and had so much fun.

00:19:18.630 --> 00:19:21.800
The blue topaz you found, Asou-san.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:23.360
Was it really here?

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.740
Yes, we found it here.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:30.890
I picked it up and analysed it.
Sorry for trespassing.

00:19:30.890 --> 00:19:35.020
Was that when you realised that Sadakichi-san
and the rest of the Seven Sages were here?

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:40.240
If you actually mine this land
and find blue topaz,

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:41.860
it's all yours.

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:44.480
Don't you and your club want it?

00:19:44.480 --> 00:19:45.760
Nope.

00:19:45.760 --> 00:19:48.160
But in return, tell Sadakichi-san I said thanks.

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.080
Tell him that the stupid junior
high girl with a death wish

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:55.000
got mad at their stupid advice
and lost the will to die.

00:19:55.620 --> 00:19:58.420
What happened to that stupid junior high girl?

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:01.170
Do I have to spell it out?

00:20:01.170 --> 00:20:04.360
The Sages will want to know.

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:07.720
Because they're still worried
about that stupid girl.

00:20:09.120 --> 00:20:10.940
Enough with the "stupid".

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:13.560
She's following their advice

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:16.570
and looking for her own light.

00:20:19.020 --> 00:20:21.030
P-Please wait!

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:23.480
No can do.

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.240
We're pitching a strike.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:27.150
You mean "going on strike"!

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:29.020
Let's read the postcard already.

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.170
No. This ends today.

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:33.440
Our final piece of advice is for you, Kaiyu.

00:20:33.440 --> 00:20:35.530
Did you go senile? Give me a break.

00:20:35.530 --> 00:20:38.430
The seven of us all agreed on this.

00:20:38.430 --> 00:20:41.100
Some friends from school
came over last night, right?

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:43.200
Let's not do this.

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:48.060
Rejoice, boy. Your father finally
found a place that'll take us in.

00:20:48.060 --> 00:20:49.570
No need to worry about us anymore.

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:50.680
But...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.050
We've been taking advantage of your kind words.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:56.230
Go back to school, Kaiyu.

00:20:56.230 --> 00:20:59.480
What will I even do there now? It's too late.

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:03.400
I heard you played the taiko
in the fife and percussion band.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:04.820
Are you talking about drums?

00:21:04.820 --> 00:21:07.740
They won't let me join now.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:12.240
I wanted to check if the snare drums
and timpani were still usable.

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:14.660
For a childhood friend.

00:21:14.660 --> 00:21:17.120
I want him to come back to school.

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:18.520
Was Serizawa-san talking about him?

00:21:18.520 --> 00:21:21.710
Don't you have any fun memories of school?

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:27.320
Well, I did have a laugh at the girl practising
the flute at the parking lot last year.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.850
My recorder skills are probably
a thousand times better.

00:21:31.290 --> 00:21:31.600
But it's too late for me to play the drums now.

00:21:31.600 --> 00:21:33.390
What the hell?
But it's too late for me to play the drums now.

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.020
I haven't touched them in ages.

00:21:36.020 --> 00:21:41.510
"It's too late" is the kind of excuse
only silly old coots like us get to use.

00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.360
A goddess has descended.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.890
Did you tune into the radio?

00:21:47.890 --> 00:21:48.610
Of course!

00:21:48.610 --> 00:21:52.530
I'm going to barge into Kaiyuu's
place right now and yell at him.

00:21:53.240 --> 00:21:55.410
I can't believe he had a laugh
at my flute playing. That jerk!

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.360
I'll go with you.

00:21:57.360 --> 00:21:59.120
The concert band's honour is riding on this!

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:01.380
This can't wait for tomorrow, can it?

00:22:01.380 --> 00:22:05.030
Time for the final episode of our lives!

00:23:31.670 --> 00:23:33.300
Step on it, you useless hacks!

00:23:33.300 --> 00:23:35.760
The privacy of your first love
will be violated all the way through.

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:36.820
You're kidding, right?

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:39.000
We're on the forest's side.

00:23:39.000 --> 00:23:40.790
Benjant is a formidable opponent.
